# Next.js pages

Public Next apps (auth, marketing, www — anything that is not a dashboard) render pages on the server.

- Default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only for interactive islands (Discord button, forms), never for a whole route.
- Every `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx` must export valid `metadata` (or `generateMetadata`) with title, description, and `metadataBase` when the app has a public URL.
- Skip icons and Open Graph images until those assets exist. Do not invent placeholder OG/favicon files.
- Dashboard apps may use client-heavy pages. Do not apply the RSC-only rule there.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client page with no metadata
"use client";
export default function Page() {
  return <h1>Sign in</h1>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — server page, metadata, client island
export const metadata = {
  title: "Sign in",
  description: "Sign in to Brigada with Discord.",
};

export default function Page() {
  return <SignInButton />;
}
```
